    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet on the beautiful island of Inishlacken, just off the coast of Roundstone in the heart of Connemara, this derelict stone cottage (on folio GY14623) occupies an exceptional coastal setting with extensive private shoreline and uninterrupted views across the Atlantic and Connemara coastline.\nPositioned above a sheltered sandy beach, the property enjoys a rare combination of privacy, natural beauty, and direct access to the sea.\nThe cottage, while requiring complete restoration (subject to any necessary planning permissions), offers a unique opportunity to revive a traditional island home in one of Ireland's most unspoilt locations. Rich in character and history, the property is ideal for those seeking a truly distinctive coastal retreat.\nThe combination of extensive shore frontage, a sandy beach at its doorstep, breathtaking sea views, and the timeless tranquillity of Inishlacken makes this a property of outstanding appeal."
      },
